## [ISSUE] Long topic titles no longer truncate in the docked header; extra-info overflows into the panel

**Severity:** HIGH -- on any topic with a long title, the docked header title overflows instead of showing an ellipsis, colliding with the notification/search/hamburger icons.

### The Problem

```scss
// header.scss:14-19
.contents {
  margin: 8px 0;
  @include flexbox();
  @include align-items(center);
}
```

`header.hbs:93-95` renders `{{header-extra-info topic=topic}}` as a direct child of `.contents`. `HeaderExtraInfo` (`components/header-extra-info.js.es6`) sets no `tagName`, so Ember wraps `<div class="extra-info-wrapper">` in an extra `<div class="ember-view">`. That wrapper div is the flex item.

The title link relies on shrinking to get an ellipsis (`desktop/topic-post.scss:518-538`):

```scss
.extra-info-wrapper { overflow: hidden; ... }
.topic-link { display: block; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
```

### Theory / Proof

CSS Flexbox Level 1, section 4.5 (Automatic Minimum Size of Flex Items): a flex item whose `overflow` is `visible` gets `min-width: auto`, which resolves to its min-content size. The flex item here is the ember-view div (overflow visible), and its min-content size includes the full `nowrap` title text. So the item cannot shrink below the title width; `overflow: hidden` on the inner `.extra-info-wrapper` does not help because it is not the flex item.

Before this PR `.title` floated left, `.panel` floated right, and `.extra-info-wrapper` was a normal block whose width was the remaining space between floats (with `overflow:hidden` establishing a BFC beside the floats), so ellipsis worked.

### What happens today vs. what will break

Short titles look fine. A title wider than the space between logo and panel overflows `.contents`; the `.panel` (auto margin, order 3) gets pushed past the right edge / overlaps, and no ellipsis appears.

### Research

This is the standard "flex item min-width: auto" pitfall documented in the spec and by CSS-Tricks ("Flexbox and Truncated Text"); the canonical fix is `min-width: 0` (or `overflow:hidden`) on the actual flex item.

### Recommendation

Make the actual flex item shrinkable, e.g. give the component a class and style it:

```js
// header-extra-info.js.es6
const TopicCategoryComponent = Ember.Component.extend({
  classNames: ['extra-info-wrapper'], // and drop the inner wrapper div from the template
```

or in CSS:

```scss
.d-header .contents > .ember-view { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; }
```

## [ISSUE] Mobile small-action custom messages now overlap the icon column

**Severity:** MEDIUM -- close/pin/etc. notices with a custom message render text on top of the action icon on mobile.

### The Problem

```scss
// common/base/topic-post.scss:279-280 (this PR)
.small-action-desc {
  padding: 0 1.5%;          // was: padding: 0.5em 0 0.5em 4em
```

but `mobile/topic-post.scss:516-523` still has:

```scss
.small-action .small-action-desc {
  .custom-message { margin-left: -40px; }
}
```

### Theory / Proof

The -40px was tuned against the old 4em left padding (4 x 0.9em x 14px ~= 50px), which left the message ~10px inside the description box, under the avatar-free area. Now the left padding is 1.5% of the containing width (~5px on a 320-375px phone), so the message starts ~35px to the left of the description box, i.e. inside the preceding `.topic-avatar` flex item that holds the 35px icon.

### What happens today vs. what will break

Small actions without a custom message are fine. Any small action post with `post.cooked` (e.g. closing a topic with a reason) renders `.custom-message` overlapping the lock/pin icon on mobile.

### Research

The desktop stylesheet has no such override, which is why this is not visible when testing on desktop.

### Recommendation

Drop or recompute the mobile override alongside this change:

```scss
// mobile/topic-post.scss
.small-action .small-action-desc {
  p { padding-top: 0; }
  // .custom-message margin-left no longer needed with flex layout
}
```

## [ISSUE] Small-action edit/delete buttons move from the row's right edge to next to the text

**Severity:** MEDIUM -- staff controls on small-action posts jump into the middle of the row.

### The Problem

```scss
.small-action {
  @include flexbox();
  @include align-items(center);
  ...
  .small-action-desc { padding: 0 1.5%; ... }
  button { float: right; ... }
```

`components/small-action.hbs` puts the delete/edit `<button>`s inside `.small-action-desc`. Before, `.small-action-desc` was a block box spanning the full `.small-action` width (755px on desktop, `desktop/topic-post.scss:730`), so `float: right` put the buttons at the far right.

### Theory / Proof

In a flex container, items default to `flex: 0 1 auto`; with `flex-basis: auto` and no width, the item's size is its max-content width (CSS Flexbox 9.2, step 3E). Floats inside it are laid out within that shrink-wrapped box, so "right" is now the right edge of the text, not of the row.

### What happens today vs. what will break

For short descriptions like "closed 2 days ago", the pencil/x buttons now sit immediately after the text instead of aligned at the right edge of the post column.

### Recommendation

Let the description take the remaining space:

```scss
.small-action-desc {
  -webkit-box-flex: 1;
  -webkit-flex: 1 1 auto;
  -ms-flex: 1 1 auto;
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  padding: 0 1.5%;
```

(ideally via a `flex($val)` mixin next to the others in `mixins.scss`).

## [GAP ANALYSIS] `align-items` mixin emits invalid legacy values/properties

**Severity:** LOW -- current callers use `center`/`baseline` (valid in all syntaxes), but the mixin silently breaks for `flex-start`/`flex-end`.

### The Problem

```scss
@mixin align-items($alignment) {
    -webkit-box-align: $alignment;
    -webkit-align-items: $alignment;
    -ms-flex-align: $alignment;
    -ms-align-items: $alignment;
    align-items:$alignment;
}
```

### Theory / Proof

- 2009 syntax `box-align` accepts `start | end | center | baseline | stretch`.
- IE10 `-ms-flex-align` accepts `start | end | center | baseline | stretch`.
- `-ms-align-items` is not a property in any IE/Edge release (IE10 used `-ms-flex-align`; IE11/Edge use unprefixed `align-items`), so it is dead output.

So `@include align-items(flex-start)` produces invalid declarations for the very browsers the prefixes target, and they fall back to `stretch`.

### Research

Autoprefixer and Bourbon's `align-items` mixin map `flex-start -> start` and `flex-end -> end` for the legacy properties.

### Recommendation

```scss
@mixin align-items($alignment) {
  $legacy: $alignment;
  @if $alignment == flex-start { $legacy: start; }
  @else if $alignment == flex-end { $legacy: end; }
  -webkit-box-align: $legacy;
  -ms-flex-align: $legacy;
  -webkit-align-items: $alignment;
  align-items: $alignment;
}
```
